=== entry d0aae5b2aecc
kind: translation
rules: setup-pstack, capabilities, model-role, cursor-only
intent: Detects models with `orchestrator_capabilities`, including each model's effort options; drops the Cursor models API and the `auto` alias. Keep "ask the user if detection fails" and "never write an unconfirmed model".
--- upstream
Enumerate the model slugs you can pass to a `Task` subagent in this session. That is the dependable source. If Cursor also exposes a models API or CLI that lists the user's entitled models, prefer it for completeness. If you cannot detect any, ask the user to paste the slugs they have access to. Never write a real slug you have not confirmed is available. The aliases `inherit-parent` and `auto` are always valid even though they are not detected slugs.
--- patched
Call `orchestrator_capabilities`. Each entry in `providers` lists a provider instance's models and each model's effort options (`effort`, or `reasoningEffort` for `codex`). That is the dependable source. A provider whose `canRunChildTask` is false can't run a role, so leave it out. If you cannot detect any, ask the user to paste the models they have access to. Never write a real model you have not confirmed is available. The alias `inherit-parent` is always valid even though it is not a detected model.

=== entry cf59bc9fbcaf
kind: translation
rules: setup-pstack, model-role
intent: Loads current choices from the project models file and its `# budget:` line, else the defaults listed in step 5. Keep the retired-role drop. Its example stays `how critics`, because the roles upstream now names as retired are still roles in models.json.
--- upstream
The default role-to-model mapping is the rule shape shown in step 5 below. If `~/.cursor/rules/pstack-models.mdc` already exists, read it and treat its `# budget` line and its role values as the current choices. Otherwise start from those defaults. A line whose role is not in step 5, such as `hardest tasks`, `architect runners`, `reflect tooling`, or `why investigators`, is from a retired role. Drop it.
--- patched
The defaults are the role entries listed in step 5 below. If that file already exists, read it and treat its `# budget:` line and its role entries as the current choices. Otherwise start from those defaults. A line whose role is not in step 5, such as `how critics`, is from a retired role. Drop it.

