=== entry 9c6961655482
kind: translation
rules: setup-pstack, model-role, model-effort
intent: A budget moves each entry's effort down from its default's (`large` keeps it, `medium` one step, `small` two), capped at `xhigh`, or the highest that model offers below the target; drops slug parsing, families, the `auto` alias, and the per-vendor slug notes (fast slugs, Gemini's ceiling). willyskills's panel defaults mix efforts, so the target is per entry, starting from the default entry for the same model. Keep "keep the user's changed roles on a re-run" and "mark a role needing a choice".
--- upstream
**(b) Apply it.** Build the working table from the skill defaults, and on a re-run keep any role you changed by family, list, or alias (`inherit-parent`, `auto`). Families are the ones Phase A of the **arena** skill defines, so Fable is its own family. Each role has a target effort, which is its default's effort moved by the budget. `large` keeps it, `medium` lowers it one step, and `small` lowers it two steps, on the ladder `xhigh` > `high` > `medium` > `low`. No role runs above `xhigh`, and a target at the bottom of the ladder stays there. Most defaults are at `xhigh`, and each budget label names where those land. Set the effort token of every real slug in the role, panel entries included, to the role's target. The effort token is the last token, or the one before a trailing `fast`. If the result is not a detected slug, use the same family's detected slug with the highest effort at or below the target, else mark the role as needing a choice. `inherit-parent` and `auto` do not change. So `medium` turns `claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-fast` into `claude-opus-5-5-high-fast` and `claude-opus-5-5-high-fast` into `claude-opus-5-5-medium-fast`, and `small` turns them into `claude-opus-5-5-medium-fast` and `claude-opus-5-5-low-fast`. Opus 5.5 always runs its `-fast` slug, so every Opus 5.5 value ends in `-fast`. Fable 5.2 and Gemini have no fast slug, so never write one. Gemini tops out at `high`, so a Gemini entry runs at `high` when its role's target is `xhigh`.
--- patched
**(b) Apply it.** Build the working table from the defaults, and on a re-run keep any role you changed by model, list, or alias (`inherit-parent`). Each real entry has a target effort: the effort of the role's default entry for the same model, else the role's highest default effort, moved by the budget. `large` keeps it, `medium` lowers it one step, and `small` lowers it two steps, on the ladder `xhigh` > `high` > `medium` > `low`. Ignore effort options off that ladder. No entry runs above `xhigh`, and a target at the bottom of the ladder stays there. Each budget label names where an `xhigh` default lands. Set the effort of every real entry, panel entries included, to its target. If the model doesn't offer that effort, use the highest effort it offers below it, else mark the role as needing a choice. `inherit-parent` does not change. So `medium` turns an `xhigh` entry into `high` and a `high` entry into `medium`, and `small` turns them into `medium` and `low`.

=== entry 72eaf27f2813
kind: translation
rules: ask, setup-pstack, model-role, cursor-only, same-model-review
intent: Confirms roles in plain text with `inherit-parent` as the only alias; drops `auto` and Cursor's Auto, and the Fable-is-Claude vendor note. Keep the `xhigh` cap on offered models, the panel-list and swarm notes, and that an alias never judges. `architect runners` stays a panel role because it is still in models.json. Policy: the cross-judge prefers another provider but falls back to the first value instead of skipping (the willyskills default pool is Opus alone), so a judge always runs.
--- upstream
**(c) Show the roles and confirm.** Show every role with its model, marking any real slug not in the detected set as needing a choice. Also list each line step 2 dropped. Ask whether to accept as-is or change specific roles, offering the detected models at `xhigh` or below plus `inherit-parent` and `auto` (both mean: this role runs on the parent chat model, which is how Auto users stay on Auto) as the options. Prefer AskQuestion over free text. For panel roles (arena runners, interrogate reviewers) the value is a list, and one subagent runs per entry, alias entries included, so the list length sets the count. `arena cross-judge pool` is also a list, but Arena runs one judge. It tries only values from a vendor other than the parent's, in list order, so order it by preference. Fable and the other Claude models are one vendor. An `inherit-parent` or `auto` value never judges. `swarm workers` is the default model for every worker unless a race or comparison assigns another model per arm.
--- patched
**(c) Show the roles and confirm.** Show every role with its entries, marking any real entry not in the detected set as needing a choice. Also list each line step 2 dropped. Ask whether to accept as-is or change specific roles, offering the detected models at `xhigh` or below plus `inherit-parent` (this role runs on the parent chat model) as the options. Ask in plain text, then end the turn. For panel roles (arena runners, architect runners, interrogate reviewers) the value is a list, and one subagent runs per entry, alias entries included, so the list length sets the count. `arena cross-judge pool` is also a list, but Arena runs one judge. It takes the first value in list order whose provider differs from the parent's, else the first value, so order it by preference. An `inherit-parent` value never judges. `swarm workers` is the default model for every worker unless a race or comparison assigns another model per arm.

